    directAnswer: "Most commercial, industrial, and multifamily projects in Louisiana require plans stamped by a Louisiana-licensed PE in responsible charge. Single-family homes are generally exempt. Parish-level permitting, coastal subsidence and hurricane rules, and New Orleans' below-sea-level drainage reality shape foundations, flood design, and the entire plan review path.",
